# Secrets Management

## Mục tiêu

Secrets Management là practices và tools để protect sensitive information như passwords, API keys, tokens, và certificates. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, secrets được managed centrally với proper access controls, rotation, và auditing. Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc handle secrets một cách secure và compliant.

Secure secrets management là critical cho security - secrets leaks can lead to data breaches, unauthorized access, và significant financial impact.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Centralized Storage**

Store secrets in dedicated system. No hardcoding. No config files in repo. Central visibility.

**2. Least Privilege**

Grant minimum access needed. Role-based access. Regular reviews. Revoke unused access.

**3. Encryption**

Encrypt at rest. Encrypt in transit. Use proper key management. Rotate encryption keys.

**4. Rotation**

Rotate secrets regularly. Automate rotation. No manual rotation. Short-lived credentials.

**5. Auditing**

Log all access. Track changes. Alert on anomalies. Compliance reporting.

**6. No Secrets in Code**

No hardcoded secrets. No in comments. No in logs. Externalize all secrets.

**7. Secrets Lifecycle**

Create. Store. Use. Rotate. Revoke. Destroy. Complete lifecycle management.

**8. Development Practices**

Different secrets per environment. Mask in logs. Limit dev access. Production isolation.

**9. Emergency Access**

Define emergency procedures. Audit emergency access. Time-limited access. Post-incident review.

**10. Backup và Recovery**

Back up secrets store. Test recovery. Document procedures. Redundancy.

## Checklist

- [ ] Secrets store configured
- [ ] Access controls defined
- [ ] Rotation policy established
- [ ] Encryption configured
- [ ] Auditing enabled
- [ ] Secrets in code removed
- [ ] Environment separation configured
- [ ] Emergency procedures documented
- [ ] Team trained on practices
- [ ] Compliance requirements met

## Anti Pattern

**1. Hardcoded Secrets**

API keys in code. Passwords in config. Secrets in git. Remove immediately.

**2. Shared Accounts**

Generic passwords. Shared credentials. No accountability. Unique credentials.

**3. No Rotation**

Same passwords for years. No key rotation. Accumulated secrets. Security debt.

**4. Over-Permission**

Admin access for everyone. Too many permissions. Access creep. Principle of least privilege.

**5. Secrets in Logs**

Passwords in logs. Tokens in requests. Sensitive data exposure. Filter secrets.

## Best Practice

**1. HashiCorp Vault Configuration**

```yaml
# vault/config.hcl
# Vault server configuration
ui = true
cluster_addr = "https://vault.internal:8201"
api_addr = "https://vault.internal:8200"

storage "consul" {
  address = "consul.internal:8500"
  path    = "vault/"
  
  # High availability
  enable_lease_renewal = true
}

# TLS configuration
listener "tcp" {
  address       = "[::]:8200"
  cluster_address  = "[::]:8201"
  tls_cert_file = "/etc/vault/tls/vault.crt"
  tls_key_file  = "/etc/vault/tls/vault.key"
  tls_min_version = "tls12"
  
  # Disable TLS for internal only (not recommended for production)
  # telemetry {
  #   unauthenticated_metrics_access = "true"
  # }
}

# Telemetry
telemetry {
  prometheus_retention_time = "30s"
  disable_hostname = true
}

# Default lease and max lease
default_max_request_duration = "10s"
max_request_duration = "60s"

# Plugin directory
plugin_directory = "/etc/vault/plugins"

# Audit logging
audit "file" {
  file_path = "/var/log/vault/audit.log"
  log_raw = true
}

# Enterprise features
# entropy "seal" {
#   algorithm = "aes256-gcm"
# }
```

**2. Vault Policies**

```hcl
# vault-policy-engineer.hcl
# Engineer policy - read access to service secrets

# Enable secrets engines
path "sys/mounts/*" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# Read database credentials
path "database/creds/engineer-*" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# Read API keys
path "secret/data/services/*" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# Read certificates
path "pki/certs/*" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# Deny all writes
path "*" {
  capabilities = ["deny"]
}
```

```hcl
# vault-policy-prod-deploy.hcl
# Production deployment - dynamic credentials

# Database dynamic credentials
path "database/creds/prod-readonly" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

path "database/creds/prod-readwrite" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# AWS dynamic credentials
path "aws/creds/prod-deploy" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}

# Kubernetes auth
path "auth/kubernetes/login" {
  capabilities = ["read"]
}
```

**3. Kubernetes Secrets with External Secrets Operator**

```yaml
# external-secrets-operator/cluster-external-secret.yaml
apiVersion: external-secrets.io/v1beta1
kind: ClusterExternalSecret
metadata:
  name: production-secrets
spec:
  secretStoreRef:
    name: vault-backend
    kind: ClusterSecretStore
  refreshInterval: 1h
  externalSecretSpec:
    secretDeletionPolicy: Delete
    target:
      name: production-secrets
      creationPolicy: Owner
    data:
      - secretKey: DATABASE_URL
        remoteRef:
          key: secret/data/production/database
          property: url
      - secretKey: REDIS_URL
        remoteRef:
          key: secret/data/production/redis
          property: url
      - secretKey: STRIPE_API_KEY
        remoteRef:
          key: secret/data/production/stripe
          property: api_key
---
apiVersion: external-secrets.io/v1beta1
kind: ClusterSecretStore
metadata:
  name: vault-backend
spec:
  provider:
    vault:
      server: "https://vault.internal:8200"
      path: "secret"
      version: "v2"
      auth:
        kubernetes:
          mountPath: "kubernetes"
          role: "external-secrets-operator"
```

